import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <h1>About this archive</h1>
  <p>
    Everything catalogued here is fiction. Each entry is an artifact from an
    alternate timeline — a letter, a telegram, a memo, a clipping, a classroom
    handout — presented as the document itself rather than as a story about it.
    The nations, institutions, and events depicted diverge from the real ones
    deliberately.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two voices share the site. The documents speak in-world. The archivist's
    notes, set below the documents in grey, are Arcade Wise speaking as
    themself.
  </p>

  <h2>Colophon</h2>
  <p>
    Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> as a static site, no
    client-side JavaScript, system fonts only. The design follows the Arcade
    house style, factbook mode: the page is a document with a small amount of
    CSS on top of it, and any ornament must be produced by the world, not
    applied to the page. Typeset form is the data — a telegram is set in
    monospace capitals because that is what a telegram is, not because it is
    dressed as one.
  </p>
</Base>
